<div class="axyum-page">
  <h2 class="axyum-page-title">Choose Your Party Role</h2>
  <p class="axyum-page-description">
    Select a party dynamic role that defines how your character contributes to the team. This is NOT your class - any class can lean into multiple roles depending on build and playstyle. Your selection will help recommend suitable classes.
  </p>

  <div class="axyum-selection-grid role-grid">
    <button type="button" class="axyum-selection-card axyum-role-select {{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 0)}}selected{{/if}}" data-action="selectRole" data-role-index="0">
      <i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i>
      <h3 class="axyum-selection-card-title">Tank (Defender)</h3>
      <p class="axyum-selection-card-desc">Frontline protector who draws fire</p>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="axyum-selection-card axyum-role-select {{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 1)}}selected{{/if}}" data-action="selectRole" data-role-index="1">
      <i class="fas fa-bolt"></i>
      <h3 class="axyum-selection-card-title">Striker (Damage Dealer)</h3>
      <p class="axyum-selection-card-desc">High-output specialist, kills key targets</p>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="axyum-selection-card axyum-role-select {{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 2)}}selected{{/if}}" data-action="selectRole" data-role-index="2">
      <i class="fas fa-chess-board"></i>
      <h3 class="axyum-selection-card-title">Controller</h3>
      <p class="axyum-selection-card-desc">Controls space, tempo, and enemy movement</p>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="axyum-selection-card axyum-role-select {{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 3)}}selected{{/if}}" data-action="selectRole" data-role-index="3">
      <i class="fas fa-hands-helping"></i>
      <h3 class="axyum-selection-card-title">Support (Buffer)</h3>
      <p class="axyum-selection-card-desc">Boosts allies through buffs and advantages</p>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="axyum-selection-card axyum-role-select {{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 4)}}selected{{/if}}" data-action="selectRole" data-role-index="4">
      <i class="fas fa-heart"></i>
      <h3 class="axyum-selection-card-title">Healer</h3>
      <p class="axyum-selection-card-desc">Triage specialist, restores and revives</p>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="axyum-selection-card axyum-role-select {{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 5)}}selected{{/if}}" data-action="selectRole" data-role-index="5">
      <i class="fas fa-tools"></i>
      <h3 class="axyum-selection-card-title">Skill Monkey</h3>
      <p class="axyum-selection-card-desc">Utility expert for exploration and traps</p>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="axyum-selection-card axyum-role-select {{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 6)}}selected{{/if}}" data-action="selectRole" data-role-index="6">
      <i class="fas fa-comment-dots"></i>
      <h3 class="axyum-selection-card-title">Face (Social Leader)</h3>
      <p class="axyum-selection-card-desc">Spokesperson, excels in diplomacy</p>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="axyum-selection-card axyum-role-select {{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 7)}}selected{{/if}}" data-action="selectRole" data-role-index="7">
      <i class="fas fa-asterisk"></i>
      <h3 class="axyum-selection-card-title">Custom / Flexible</h3>
      <p class="axyum-selection-card-desc">Show all classes without filtering</p>
    </button>
  </div>

  {{#if (ne selectedRoleIndex null)}}
    <div class="role-detail-panel">
      <h3>{{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 0)}}Tank (Defender){{else}}{{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 1)}}Striker (Damage Dealer){{else}}{{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 2)}}Controller{{else}}{{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 3)}}Support (Buffer & Enhancer){{else}}{{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 4)}}Healer{{else}}{{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 5)}}Skill Monkey{{else}}{{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 6)}}Face (Social Leader){{else}}Custom / Flexible{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}</h3>
      
      {{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 0)}}
        <p class="role-concept"><strong>Core Concept:</strong> The frontline protector. A tank's job is to draw enemy attention, soak up damage, and prevent weaker allies from getting hit.</p>
        <p><strong>Typical Traits:</strong> Extremely high AC and HP. Defensive features that impose disadvantage, impose conditions, or reduce damage. Often occupies choke points or engages multiple foes at once.</p>
        <p><strong>Tactics:</strong> Forces enemies to focus attacks on them via Compelled Duel, Sentinel, or Reckless Attack. Provides zone control through physical positioning or mechanics that punish disengagement.</p>
        <p><strong>Example Classes/Subclasses:</strong> Fighter (Champion, Battle Master, Cavalier), Paladin (Any oath), Barbarian (Bear Totem or Zealot)</p>
        <p><strong>In the Party:</strong> Keeps enemies off squishier allies and stabilizes chaotic fights.</p>
      {{else}}{{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 1)}}
        <p class="role-concept"><strong>Core Concept:</strong> The high-output specialist who focuses on killing key targets fast.</p>
        <p><strong>Typical Traits:</strong> Exceptional damage per round (DPR), often through advantage stacking or extra attacks/spells. Usually has weaker defenses but excels in action economy - bonus actions, reactions, etc. May specialize in burst damage (nova rounds) or consistent precision attacks.</p>
        <p><strong>Tactics:</strong> Focuses on high-value targets (enemy casters, leaders). Times abilities around allies' control setups for lethal combos.</p>
        <p><strong>Example Classes/Subclasses:</strong> Rogue (Assassin or Swashbuckler), Ranger (Gloom Stalker or Hunter), Fighter (Champion or Samurai), Sorcerer (Draconic or Shadow)</p>
        <p><strong>In the Party:</strong> They end threats quickly, reducing incoming damage for everyone else.</p>
      {{else}}{{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 2)}}
        <p class="role-concept"><strong>Core Concept:</strong> Controls space, tempo, and enemy movement - the tactician's role.</p>
        <p><strong>Typical Traits:</strong> Spells or effects that restrict movement, reduce visibility, or cause status effects. High area-of-effect coverage and burst positioning effects like Entangle, Web, or Wall of Force. Good battlefield awareness; thrives on predicting enemy behavior.</p>
        <p><strong>Tactics:</strong> Shapes encounters by cutting off escapes, funneling enemies, or locking down powerful foes. Combines well with Tanks who can hold enemies in zones like Spirit Guardians or Spike Growth.</p>
        <p><strong>Example Classes/Subclasses:</strong> Wizard (Evocation or Conjuration), Druid (Land or Moon), Cleric (Tempest or Light)</p>
        <p><strong>In the Party:</strong> Keeps the battlefield manageable while the team picks off enemies efficiently.</p>
      {{else}}{{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 3)}}
        <p class="role-concept"><strong>Core Concept:</strong> Boosts allies' performance through buffs, advantages, and resource management.</p>
        <p><strong>Typical Traits:</strong> Features that enhance attack rolls, saving throws, or provide temporary HP. Highly synergistic - thrives when all allies coordinate. Often provides utility outside combat (e.g., inspiration, guidance, or ritual casting).</p>
        <p><strong>Tactics:</strong> Uses spells like Bless, Heroism, or Haste to empower allies. Manages concentration to sustain key effects over multiple rounds.</p>
        <p><strong>Example Classes/Subclasses:</strong> Bard (College of Lore or Valor), Cleric (Life, Peace, or Twilight), Paladin (Ancients or Devotion)</p>
        <p><strong>In the Party:</strong> Makes everyone else more effective, turning good rolls into great ones.</p>
      {{else}}{{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 4)}}
        <p class="role-concept"><strong>Core Concept:</strong> The party's triage specialist - restores HP, removes conditions, and keeps the group alive through tough encounters.</p>
        <p><strong>Typical Traits:</strong> Spells for restoration, protection, and revival (Healing Word, Lesser Restoration, Revivify). Deep understanding of resource economy and timing: when to heal, when to push damage instead. Often overlaps with Support but focuses on reactive aid over proactive buffs.</p>
        <p><strong>Tactics:</strong> Keeps key allies alive during focus fire scenarios. Preemptive use of spells and positioning to prevent downed states.</p>
        <p><strong>Example Classes/Subclasses:</strong> Cleric (Life, Grave, or Order), Druid (Dreams), Paladin (Lay on Hands and Aura Protection)</p>
        <p><strong>In the Party:</strong> Enables extended adventuring and recovers from tactical mistakes.</p>
      {{else}}{{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 5)}}
        <p class="role-concept"><strong>Core Concept:</strong> The utility expert - handles exploration, infiltration, traps, and problem-solving outside raw combat.</p>
        <p><strong>Typical Traits:</strong> High Dexterity or Intelligence, lots of skill proficiencies, often Expertise in key skills. Can function as a scout, investigator, or trap-springer. Always has a tool, plan, or workaround ready.</p>
        <p><strong>Tactics:</strong> Uses stealth or investigation to give the party an upper hand before battle. Provides critical information, shortcuts, or tactical setup advantages.</p>
        <p><strong>Example Classes/Subclasses:</strong> Rogue (Thief, Arcane Trickster), Bard (Lore), Ranger (Gloom Stalker)</p>
        <p><strong>In the Party:</strong> Keeps exploration efficient and prevents ambushes, saves spell slots for others.</p>
      {{else}}{{#if (eq selectedRoleIndex 6)}}
        <p class="role-concept"><strong>Core Concept:</strong> The spokesperson - excels in persuasion, deception, intimidation, and negotiation.</p>
        <p><strong>Typical Traits:</strong> High Charisma, proficiency in social skills. Strong RP drive - guides the story through dialog choices and diplomacy. Often overlaps with Support or Skill Monkey roles.</p>
        <p><strong>Tactics:</strong> Talks the party into or out of trouble, securing allies, deals, or information. Can shift entire campaigns through roleplay influence.</p>
        <p><strong>Example Classes/Subclasses:</strong> Bard (any), Paladin (Devotion or Ancients), Warlock (Fiend or Archfey), Sorcerer (Divine Soul or Enchanter)</p>
        <p><strong>In the Party:</strong> Owns social encounters and reduces the need for combat through words.</p>
      {{else}}
        <p class="role-concept"><strong>Flexible Approach:</strong> You prefer to explore all options without role-based recommendations. All classes will be shown on the next page.</p>
        <p><strong>Note:</strong> Many builds can flex between two or three roles - for example, a Bard might cover Support + Face + Skill Monkey, while a Paladin might handle Tank + Support + Healer.</p>
      {{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}{{/if}}
    </div>
  {{/if}}

  <div style="margin-top: 2rem;">
    <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--axyum-accent);">
      <em>Note: A well-balanced party typically covers at least 4 of these roles. Role selection will filter recommended classes on the next page.</em>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
